{"reference":"Psalms 120","book":"Psalms","chapter":120,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Psalms That Follow","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One reading of the wider sequence sees these psalms as preserving communal memory of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile while also gathering thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and Songs of Ascents oriented toward worship.","verse_refs":["Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_120_54f9dc97543abc612fa7c33a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}